    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d483-a1">

                <pb facs="0579" n="495" xml:id="pg495"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Choate to Lord Lansdowne.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1903-03-19"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">March 19,
                    1903</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord</hi>: I have the honor to inclose herewith
                    copies (2) of the President’s proclamation of the convention between the United
                    States and Great Britain for the settlement of questions between the two
                    countries with respect to the boundary line between Alaska and the British
                    possessions in North America, signed at Washington January 24, 1903, and to
                    inform your lordship that the President has appointed the Hon. Elihu Root,
                    Secretary of War of the United States, the Hon. Henry Cabot Lodge, the Senator
                    for Massachusetts, the Hon. George Turner, ex-Senator of the State of
                    Washington, as American members of the tribunal provided for in the
                    convention.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Joseph H. Choate.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
